smiley for OS-9/68000=====================ORIG holds comp.sources.misc volume 23, smiley version 4 patchlevel 0,as posted.  The files beside it build the OS-9 program.What changed, and why:  smiley.c   A value returned from main reaches the shell as 0 here             (measured: `return 3' gives 0, `exit(3)' gives 3), and             smiley reports the number of smileys it did not know that             way.  Under OSK main is renamed smiley_main and a new main             passes its value to exit().  Nothing else is changed.  faces.c    Generated, as the Makefile does, by `sort faces.in | mkfaces',             run on OS-9 with the disk's sort and mkfaces built from             ORIG/mkfaces.c.  Its entries are in strcmp order, which the             bsearch lookup needs; checked byte for byte against the same             two steps done in the C locale.getopt.c, ltoa.c, bsearch.c, mkfaces.c, smiley.h and patchlevel.h buildunchanged from ORIG.  ORIG/other.uu is the author's set of multi-linesmileys, left encoded as posted.Build: cc smiley.c faces.c getopt.c ltoa.c bsearch.c -DOSK